$ enola diff --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola diff [flags] <revA>..<revB> [repo_path|config_path]

Show the architecture delta between two recorded revisions.

Each side is a snapshot id or its prefix, a git commit, HEAD~N, @<seq>, a ref
name, or `latest`. An omitted side means the oldest (left) or newest (right).

With a shared store (--store, or history.shared_dir) both sides resolve over
the union of the local history and the store, and the header names where
each side came from.

Flags:
  -focus string
    	narrow the delta to entries referencing this module, file or symbol
  -json
    	emit the delta as JSON
  -store string
    	also resolve revisions from a shared history store (default: history.shared_dir)
